accession number   removed_accession_id  report status  final type  surgical pathology pathology report   removed_accession_id  operation date  30 may 95 accessioned on  30 may 95 at 13 20 clinical data  right breast mass                                                                                      final diagnosis     breast  right   excision  1  infiltrating ductal carcinoma grade removed_date  99     see note  2  ductal carcinoma in situ  solid type  1    note  histologically  focal signet ring cell formation is present  a prominent eosinophilic inflammatory cell response is observed  the carcinoma measures 2 4cm in greatest diameter on histologic section  slide e  and extends to the inked resection margin  vascular and lymphatic invasion are not identified  the frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  hormone receptor analysis will be reported in an addendum  diagnosis by  elizabeth bailey  md signed on  03 removed_month 95 at 10 57                                                                                     receptor immunohistochemistry addendum     results of staining of fixed tissue for hormone receptor proteins breast  right   the tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  the tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  see note  note  in this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  when we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   in this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  the results of immunohistochemical staining for progesterone receptor protein are for investigational use only  they must not be used for clinical purposes  added by  frederick carl koerner  m d  signed on  14 removed_month 95 at 13 33 gross description  received fresh in the frozen section lab   labeled remove_patient_name  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast mass   is a removed_date x removed_date x 1 9cm firm  tan to yellow piece of fibroadipose tissue which is inked and sectioned to reveal a removed_date x removed_date x 0 9cm white  hard  stellate area  a representative section from this area is frozen as fx 1  and saved frozen  the remainder of the specimen is submitted entirely in a through l  resident  james j  tiesinga  md     intra operative diagnosis     frozen section diagnosis  1  right breast  invasive carcinoma  o r  resident  ross c  wheeler  md o r  diagnosis by  judith ann ferry  m d                                                                                  source care unit  same day surgical unit    removed_accession_id  reports to  edwin lee carter  m d  ross charles wheeler  m d  judith ann ferry  m d  part   right breast mass   report_end  , Positive.
